  "note": "Borough election, 16 May 1938. There was no contest; the sixteen members of the new council were returned unopposed. The first annual meeting of the new borough council names the full sixteen members in order (Northern Herald, 28 May 1938, p. 6, read from the page image): W. H. Simms, Robert Edgar, William M'Alpine, Robert J. Beckett, Isaac Baxter, S. J. M'Watters, William Higson, Robert Morrow, J. Martin Poots, Hugh M. Donaldson, John R. Smyth, Robert George, John J. Black, T. A. Brett, Senator T. R. Lavery and Captain James M'Morran. W. H. Simms was elected first Mayor and Robert Edgar, R. J. Beckett, Senator T. R. Lavery and Robert George were appointed aldermen. The report records that the charter incorporating Newtownards as a borough was granted by letters patent dated 8 November 1937. The Belfast Telegraph of 7 May 1938 records that withdrawals in Castle, Scrabo, Victoria and Glen wards left sixteen members for the sixteen seats. The paper's ward-by-ward list is incomplete, so the return is recorded for the borough as a whole rather than guessing ward allocations. Returned unopposed."
